HILL CANNON — REPRODUCTION SPEC
================================
Single-file Python 3 game. Dependencies: pygame, numpy.
Goal: another LLM/developer can rebuild the same game from this spec alone.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PURPOSE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Artillery game. Player cannon sits on a hill at LEFT. A dense city fills the
rest of the screen. Destroy >= 50% of the city before the player's cannon is
destroyed (10 hits).

Win:  destroyed_ratio >= 0.50
Lose: player_hp reaches 0
Restart after game over: R
Quit: Esc or window close

destroyed_ratio:
  Each fully destroyed building (alive==False or fall >= height) is worth 1.
  If that building was the air-raid-siren building when it died (counted_double),
  it is worth 2.
  ratio = points / total_building_count

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. TECH / WINDOW
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Internal sim size: 1280 x 720. Draw everything to an off-screen Surface of
that size, then pygame.transform.smoothscale onto the real window.

Window: pygame.RESIZABLE, min 640x360.
Persist {x,y,w,h} as JSON in shells_window.json next to the script.
On launch, BEFORE set_mode, set os.environ["SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS"] = "x,y"
from the saved file (default 80,60,1280,720).
Save on VIDEORESIZE, WINDOWMOVED, every ~2 seconds, and on quit.

Caption: "Hill Cannon — Level the City"
FPS 60. pygame.mixer stereo 22050 Hz, 24 channels.

HUD bottom: "Destroyed xx.x% / 50%   Guns N   Force F   Bombs B   B=A-bomb"
HUD top-left: 10 HP pips (red if remaining), "Force" + 3 yellow pips,
              "A-bombs" + 3 green pips (dim if spent).

Game-over banner center-top: "CITY FALLEN — YOU WIN" or
"CANNON DESTROYED — YOU LOSE" plus "Press R to rebuild the city   ESC to quit".
On hit-player, brief red full-screen flash (~0.25s).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WORLD
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GROUND_Y = 650
Sky: vertical gradient dark blue.
Distant darker building silhouettes behind the playable city.
Ground: green-brown strip; 6px lighter lip at GROUND_Y.
Hill: filled polygon on the LEFT ending near x=200.
Player mount: hill_peak = (90, GROUND_Y - 210). Cannon about 1.5x higher than
typical mid-rises.

City starts x=210, packed to W-30.
Each building:
  width random 22-48
  gap 4-14
  stories random 1-40
  story_h = 14
  height = stories * 14
  y = GROUND_Y - height
  muted gray/brown/slate colors, darker 6px right edge
  window grid: 6x8 px, ~12 px columns; some lit (220,210,140), some dark

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. CONTROLS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Left / Up arrows     : raise barrel (decrease angle)
Right / Down arrows  : lower barrel (increase angle)
Angle clamp          : about -0.95*pi .. +0.15 rad
                       (0 = right, negative = up)
1 / 2 / 3            : muzzle force levels
Space                : fire normal shell (3 per second, cooldown 1/3 s)
B                    : fire A-bomb (same cooldown, max 3 per city; ignore if 0)
R                    : after game over, rebuild city, reset HP=10, bombs=3,
                       force=2, angle=-0.55, clear particles/shells/chunks,
                       new siren + air-raid loop, place starting guns

Force muzzle speeds:
  1 = 430 px/s   (close)
  2 = 640 px/s   (mid, default)
  3 = 920 px/s   (far rooftops)

Gravity on all shells: +520 px/s^2 on vy each frame.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. PLAYER CANNON
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Draw: dark circle mount + thick barrel line 40px along current angle +
gold muzzle tip.
HP 10. Enemy shell whose center is within 38 px of hill_peak counts as a hit.
Player shells do not hurt the player.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. SHELLS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Integrate: vy += GRAVITY*dt; x += vx*dt; y += vy*dt.
Die if off-screen or y >= GROUND_Y (ground burst + boom).

Normal player shell: small bright gold circle, short gold trail.
Enemy shell: red/orange, same size.
A-bomb: SAME ballistics as a normal player shell at current force.
  LOOKS different and larger:
  - pulsing green core (~8-12 px) with lime highlight
  - dark-green fins
  - long green spark trail
  - occasional green/yellow spark particles while in flight

Collision order per shell per frame:
  1) ground
  2) player mount (enemy shells only)
  3) air-raid SIREN hitbox if present (any shell)
  4) rooftop GUN hitbox (non-bomb shells)
  5) building body rect

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. BUILDINGS — DAMAGE AND LIGHTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hits to destroy a building (body shots): 5.
First hits draw crack lines; lights near impact may:
  - go out
  - flicker
  - dim to 25%-75% brightness
Sometimes several floors black out.
Chance the WHOLE building blacks out, higher when 1-2 hits from collapse
  (~8% normal, ~38% at 2 remaining, ~55% at 1 remaining).
On hit, ~55% chance a small fire (ember) appears near impact for 5-10 seconds.

Direct hit on rooftop GUN: instant destroy (cannon-kill).
Direct hit on SIREN: instant destroy + double score + stop air-raid +
  topple with extra smash power.

On any kill:
  10% chance the building TOPPLES (same as A-bomb topple).
  A-bomb and siren kills ALWAYS topple.
  Other kills usually pancake-drop straight down with dust at the base.
  ~25% of non-topple kills (and gun/bomb kills) become fiery explosions.

Pancake fall: building sinks straight down; dust/smoke at base; gone when
fall >= height.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. TOPPLE (A-BOMB, SIREN, OR 10% OF NORMAL KILLS)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Choose direction:
  From impact x vs building center, else toward the side with more buildings.

Split the facade into horizontal slabs (~2 stories tall).
Each slab becomes a Chunk:
  vx in topple direction (stronger for higher slabs)
  slight upward/random vy
  spin in fall direction
  gravity, bounce weakly on ground, emit smoke/junk particles
  rumble + explosion sounds

Neighbor damage by CITY INDEX distance (sort buildings by center-x):
  Adjacent (1 building away, same direction as fall):
    several body hits (power 3, or 5 if A-bomb, doubled again if siren kill)
    A-bomb/siren may chain-topple adjacent (~40% if power >= 5)
  1-2 buildings beyond that (index distance 2 or 3):
    light only: either TWO electrical-arc fires OR ONE regular body hit
  Farther: no smash damage

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. ELECTRICAL ARCING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
After a body hit, ~22% chance the damaged living building starts arcing.
While arcing, every 3-5 seconds zap a spatially adjacent living neighbor:
  jagged lightning polyline, zap sound.
  ~72% of bolts start a fire on the target (ember + small fireburst).
  4 such arc-fires on one building = 1 equivalent shell hit
  (then lights/arc-start roll as a normal hit).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10. ENEMY GUNS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Count scales with destruction toward 50%:
  at 0% destroyed: 2 guns
  at 50%+:         5 guns
  interpolate and round between.

When a gun is PLACED on a roof:
  silent 4-8 seconds (gun_cd random 4..8) before it may fire.
  After that, fire interval = 1.4 seconds (40% slower than 1/s).
  Prefer placing new guns on the TALLEST living buildings that lack a gun.
  If a gun-building dies, replace to keep the target count.

Aiming:
  Barrel may rotate any angle 0-360 but MUST face the player's cannon
  (dot product of barrel dir vs vector-to-hill_peak > 0.05).
  Never fire the opposite way.
  Independently pick force 1/2/3 (same speeds as player).
  Simulate ballistic arcs; if the path hits another living building first,
  do NOT fire; keep slewing elevation to find a clear loft.
  If a gun's own shells have hit friendly buildings 3 times, HOLD FIRE
  until a simulated path can reach the player without hitting the city.

Accuracy when they do fire:
  Base chance to use the exact ballistic solution = 1 / 7
  (that is 1-in-3.5, then halved).
  Scale that chance by building height:
    40 stories: * 0.98
    20 stories: * 0.50
    10 stories: * 0.25
    1 story:    * ~0.12
    interpolate between those anchors.
  Missed shots add angle jitter but still must face the player and must not
  be predicted to hit friendly buildings.

Visual: small dark mount + barrel + gold tip on the roof.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11. AIR-RAID SIREN
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Exactly ONE building per city (prefer stories >= 12) has a red rooftop siren:
  flashing red lamp, horn fins, dark base.
  Hitbox ~22x24 above the roof.

On city create: start a LOOPING rising/falling civil-defense wail
(sine sweep ~420-800 Hz over ~3.2s, looped, modest volume).
Stop the wail when that building is destroyed, on win, on lose, on quit.
Hitting the siren destroys the building immediately, counts 2x toward the
50% goal, topples it, and applies doubled smash power to neighbors.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12. A-BOMBS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3 per city. B fires one if any remain (same cooldown and ballistics as Space).
One A-bomb hit destroys the building in a single shot and ALWAYS topples it.
Unlimited is NOT allowed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
13. AUDIO (procedural, vary each play)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build several variants of each SFX with NumPy and pick at random + slight
volume jitter.

Cannon: low 30-70 Hz boom + 25-45ms noise muzzle crack + faint 380-560 Hz ring.
Explosion / shell impact: crack then long bass rumble + debris noise.
Collapse: grind + thud.
Topple rumble: deeper, longer (0.9-1.4s) 16-28 Hz + mid + noise.
Arc: harsh AM buzz 900-1600 Hz + hiss + random pops.
Air raid: looping sweep described above.
Hit-player: dull 36 Hz + noise.
Fireball/whoosh for fiery collapses.
Win/lose: reuse a cannon/explosion sting.

Stereo arrays (N,2) int16 for pygame.sndarray.make_sound.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
14. PARTICLES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Generic dots with optional gravity.
Bursts on muzzle, impacts, ground, collapse.
Embers: local to a building face, flicker 5-10s, spawn rising sparks.
Chunks: rotating slabs from topples (see §8).
Bolts: short-lived polylines.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
15. MAIN LOOP ORDER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
events -> aim keys -> cooldowns ->
ensure_cannons -> update buildings (and maybe fire) ->
update shells -> collide ->
update embers/particles/bolts/chunks ->
draw bg, buildings, chunks, embers, bolts, shells, particles, player cannon,
HUD, flash, game-over -> present scaled -> occasional geom save.

Do not spawn extra guns or fire after game_over except remaining fall anims.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16. RESET / NEW CITY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rebuild buildings from scratch, pick a new siren, start air-raid,
clear shells/particles/embers/bolts/chunks,
player_hp=10, bombs_left=3, force=2, angle=-0.55, player_cd=0,
place 2 guns on tallest roofs with 4-8s silence.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
17. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- One file is fine.
- Building.alive False and fall>=height both mean "gone" for scoring and
  collision; still allow pancake animation if not a topple.
- smash_neighbors uses index-distance on buildings sorted by center x,
  only in the topple direction.
- Player and bomb shells share one cooldown.
- Enemy "silent after place" is just a long initial gun_cd; after first
  eligible shot, gun_cd = 1.4.
- Window scale is visual only; all physics stay in 1280x720 space.